						<div style="width:100%;">
							<p class="MsoNormal" align="center"><i><b><font face="Georgia" color="#0000ff" size="6"><span style="COLOR: blue"></span></font></b></i><span style="COLOR: blue"></span></p> <div class="MsoNormal" style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: blue"> <hr align="center" width="100%" size="2" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">&nbsp;<span style="COLOR: blue">All members, potential and existing, are to read the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1036">New Members</a> page as well as the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1035">Rules and Regulations</a>.&nbsp; New and existing members also are to read the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1539">Our Officers</a> and <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1440">Raid Rules</a>&nbsp;pages.</span><?xml:namespace prefix = o /><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">New members gain&nbsp;DKP just like established members. However, new members cannot vote on raid or guild bank items, until they have been with the guild for 30 days.&nbsp; (The exceptions to this rule are listed under the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1035">Rules and Regulations</a>)<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">New members cannot become officers or raid looters during their 30-day probationary period. <o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">If a person would like to join Moonlite Redemption, they can apply at the website by filling out the <a href="/application.aspx">application</a>.&nbsp; Tell us a little about yourself such as your character name, class and level, as well as why you would like to join MR, etc.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">We take characters of all races and classes. The minimum level requirement is 55, excluding alts. <o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">A full member must sponsor new members during their probationary period. The sponsor is responsible for reporting any misconduct, and making sure that new members understand the guild rules and regulations. <o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">Reports of misconduct may result in immediate removal. All probationary members are subject to removal with or without previous notification or reason. </span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">All members need to make sure that the guild/site leader has their email address.&nbsp; The site email address is: moonlite_redemption@yahoo.com<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" align="center"><span style="COLOR: blue"><i><b><font face="Georgia" size="5">Prerequisites for New Members</font></b></i><o:p></o:p></span></p> <div class="MsoNormal" style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><span style="COLOR: blue"> <hr align="center" width="100%" size="2" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">New members must be level <strong>55</strong> or above. This does not apply to current members' alternate characters. <o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">All new members&nbsp;must be sponsored&nbsp;by an existing full member.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"></span><span style="COLOR: blue">New members must read and follow the<a href="../custom.aspx?pid=1035"><span style="COLOR: blue; TEXT-DECORATION: none"> Rules and Regulations</span></a>.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue">Applications will be reviewed and applicants will receive an answer either in game or&nbsp;email.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"></span><span style="COLOR: blue">The recruiting officer or guild leaders, on a probationary status, will invite qualified applicants to the guild.<o:p></o:p></span></p><span style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: blue; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'">One month after joining, the sponsor, class officers and guild leaders will discuss the new member and determine whether the member is ready for full membership.&nbsp; The member’s “joined date” will be removed from the guild manager when full membership is granted.</span>
							
